description:
Overview:

Trimac isn't just a transportation company; it's an industry disruptor with a remarkable 80-year legacy of safely delivering products that improve people’s lives across North America.

Our workplace culture is centered on being safe, respectful, innovative and inclusive. We are committed to maintaining a rewarding work environment that allows employees to experience new opportunities and build their chosen careers. Across the company, we encourage open communication, champion integrity, celebrate individuality and cultivate diverse talents and perspectives. If you’re ready for a challenge that will help drive forward an industry leading team, we invite you to begin your journey with us.

Pay Details:

Compensation for this position is determined based on experience, market data, and other relevant factors considered at the time of offer. The salary range for this role is **$82,000 to $135,000**; however, compensation may fall outside of this range depending on the candidate's qualifications, experience, and overall circumstances.

Job Details:

The Terminal Manager is the primary point of contact for Drivers to assist in solving problems and answering questions in a timely and effective manner while also facilitating the safe and professional performance of their work. The Terminal Manager is responsible for the operational as well as financial performance of their terminal(s) and collaborates with the Area Manager to assist with the development of the terminal budget so that they have a full understanding of expected deliverables. This position also manages local customer relationships and any issues that may affect profitability.

This role reports to a Director, Area Operations and interacts with Company Drivers, Independent Contractors, Service Centers, management, Safety, Human Resources, and local customers.

Who You Are:

* Strong knowledge of the transportation industry is an asset;
* Strong communicator with excellent interpersonal and coaching skills;
* Self-motivated and able to work productively with minimal supervision;
* High moral integrity;
* Strong analytical ability with good judgement;
* Proactive and decisive when making decisions;

Responsibilities:

**SAFETY:**

* Collaborate with the Safety Trainer to identify, review and address safety events;
* Lead safety and driver meetings at the terminal;
* Reviewing in-cab camera events with the Safety Trainers for potential coaching or remediation;
* Provide clarity on safety expectations and procedures and work with the Safety department to provide coaching, training and remediation as necessary;
* Final escalation point for Safety violations;
* Review safety reports and analytical data and address any issues or trends;
* Ensure the terminal has the appropriate safety supplies;
* Ensure all equipment meets regularity and corporate compliance;
* Promote a proactive safety culture within the terminal and enforce a culture of safety through actions and communications;
* Ensure the terminal is organized, clean and free of safety hazards;
* Work with Dispatch Managers to monitor high risk weather conditions and in conjunction with Area Managers evaluate if conditions allow for safe travel.

**D****RIVERS****:**

* Primary point of contact for responding to and creating solutions for driver complaints, concerns, and questions;
* Coach and mentor Drivers with an emphasis on open communication;
* Set measurable goals with Drivers and maintain accountability and performance manage as needed;
* Work with Recruiting and Sales departments to ensure proper driver levels based on revenue projections, new business, and projected turnover;
* Work collaboratively with the Service Centers to ensure efficient and fair dispatching of eligible Drivers based on availability;
* Support driver retention, engagement and satisfaction and working with Human Resources on corresponding initiatives;
* Understand and uphold Independent Contractors' contracts and understand and apply local collective bargaining agreements, where applicable
* Working collaboratively across the Company to understand company policies & procedures and ensure compliance;
* Assisting with the onboarding of new Drivers, their associated paperwork and any necessary follow-ups.

**RESOURCE** **UTILIZATION**

* Monitor and control asset utilization;
* Determine driver utilization expectations, parameters and controls and communicate them to services centres so that issues and/or trends are identified and appropriate levels are determined for profitability;
* Perform fleet planning projections and ensure the terminal has the correct amount of assets to properly handle business opportunities;
* Works in conjunction with service centres to identify equipment due for scheduled maintenance or equipment requiring repair and coordinate the servicing of equipment with shop personnel;
* Works to ensure equipment is scheduled with shop and washrack to expediate fleet readiness and fleet planning;

